{"id": "sevt_01Fz9aLPxcPx9gTV19qh1DmP", "content": [{"text": "Confirmed. Here's the picture:\n\n**Evidence**\n- Deploy `a3f9c21` (checkout, \"refactor order summary builder\") landed **14:31:18**. Checkout p99 jumped from ~75ms to ~3,800ms+ at **14:31** \u2014 same minute.\n- The diff replaced a single batched query (`OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=ids)`) with a per-order query inside the loop \u2192 **N+1 query pattern** (runbook's #1 offender).\n- Log confirms: per-row `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` queries begin exactly at 14:31:18; one request fires ~15 of them. 3,320 such queries total.\n- The 500s are `PoolTimeout` on `/api/checkout/validate` \u2014 the N+1 exhausts the DB connection pool, and requests that can't get a connection error out (error_rate climbs from 14:40 as the pool saturates).\n\n**Fix:** revert/patch `build_summary` back to the batched `order_id__in` fetch with in-memory grouping.\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the order-summary refactor turned a single batched item query into a per-order query (N+1), saturating the checkout DB pool and causing PoolTimeout 500s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T04:50:55.298669Z", "type": "agent.message"}
